{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/group(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"extendedModule":"WorldModule","roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"title":"group(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"group","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<each ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(repeat (each ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":").Type)","kind":"text"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"Group.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Group.swift#L70"},"externalID":"s:11WorldModule0A0V5groupyyxmxQpRvzAA9ComponentRzlF","symbolKind":"method"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Keeps the given component types packed in the same order, so that queries and updates of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly these types visit their entities without lookups.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"mutating","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"group","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<each ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"types","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": repeat (each ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":").Type) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" repeat each ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Component","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule9ComponentP","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Component"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The component types to keep packed together.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"types"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A query of several types normally walks one type’s storage and looks up the entity in each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the others. After you group the types, the entities that hold all of them sit at the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"front of each type’s storage, at the same positions, and spawning, inserting, removing and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"despawning keep them there. A query of the same types in any order, or an update that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writes and reads exactly those types, walks that front directly.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use a group for a set of types you visit together on every step, such as position and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"velocity:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["var world = World()","let comet = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 2))","world.spawn(Position(x: 9, y: 9))","world.group(Position.self, Velocity.self)","","world.update(Position.self, reading: Velocity.self) { position, row in","    position.x += row.components.dx","    position.y += row.components.dy","}","print(world[Position.self, of: comet])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 2.0)\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Grouping doesn’t change which entities a query or update visits, only how it finds them."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It does change the order queries list entities in, and makes adding and removing the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"grouped types a little slower. Each type belongs to at most one group. A copy of the world"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keeps the group; a snapshot doesn’t."}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":"·","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"t","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":") for ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" entities in the smallest of the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"t","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" types.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Complexity"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"types","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists at least two distinct types, and no other group owns any of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them. The checked spelling, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/group(checked:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", throws instead.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Precondition"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/world\/group(_:)"]}],"sections":[],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/group(checked:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/cache(_:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/index(_:)-u1gw","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/index(_:)-2gtfg","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/lookup(_:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/lookup(_:equals:)"],"title":"Speeding Up Queries","generated":true,"anchor":"Speeding-Up-Queries"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/docume